{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/526167-different-primal-urges-in-basu-im-would-lead-to-dead-pack-members","id":526167,"title":"Different Primal Urges in Basu-Im would lead to dead pack members?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-23T18:29:59-07:00","id":526167,"title":"Different Primal Urges in Basu-Im would lead to dead pack members?","content":"If a pack of werewolves go into Basu-Im together (because one did and the others follow suit), is it reasonable to assume that the ones with the lowest Primal Urge might get torn apart by their pack mates since they fall out of Basu-Im first and would be seen as prey by the others still in the rage? This could take the horror of Deathrage to a whole new level as other pack mates become casualties when &quot;putting it on the line&quot;. Would this be a legitimate possibility?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T19:13:09-07:00","id":526215,"title":"","content":"Maybe under some extreme circumstances, for instance if all the characters were trapped in an area and several minutes of gauru in kuruth isn't able to break them out.<br /> <br /> Presumably after ten minutes there are no other opponents, but after the opponents are gone they start doing property damage or looking for fresh meat. I'd expect the 'pack' to split up at this point, rather than a bunch of gauru taking turns hitting the same car before moving on to the next one.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't rule it out but I wouldn't think it was common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T19:25:09-07:00","id":526225,"title":"","content":"I figured that the pack would hunt as a pack together, or would they go their separate ways?<br /> <br /> I would imagine that any wolf blooded and human pack members would be casualties. In addition, any pack members that did not give into Basu-Im would have a hard time surviving. In addition, on a related topic, does the Deathrage still cause massive outrage and animosity against spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T20:24:11-07:00","id":526297,"title":"","content":"I think if there's no actual prey, they're likely to just try to find some on their own, not necessarily in a group. But like I said, it wouldn't exactly be unheard of.<br /> <br /> And yes, wolf-blooded and humans would certainly be casualties, which is why they're not often brought along on hunt. They're capable of being casualties outside of kuruth, as many werewolf antagonists are strong and brutal and silver bullets will rend human flesh just as easily as werewolf. A packmate who manages to resist their death rage might just go into gauru or use whatever skills they have to escape. Urshul form is nice, but there's plenty of gifts. An elodoth could just break one of them out of it.<br /> <br /> No, it doesn't cause any particular hatred towards spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T00:19:42-07:00","id":526445,"title":"","content":"I could have sworn that I read somewhere that they didn't attack packmates. I could be wrong, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5309-chancetr","name":"ChanceTR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T01:41:20-07:00","id":526460,"title":"","content":"'He will happily attack packmates.' But they won't attack other werewolves in Basu-Im. Which was maryshelly's issue, since Basu-Im lasts different lengths for wolves of different Primal Urge, so some packmates could drop out of it before their more long-lasting brethren.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T03:31:27-07:00","id":526511,"title":"","content":"The intention is packmates coming out of Badu-Im collapse in exhaustion, are clearly not a threat, and are largely ignored by their still rampaging packmates in favour of more interesting targets or scenery.<br /> <br /> <i>However</i>, a very clever and resourceful enemy could trap the packmates together with nothing else to focus on*, and they'd probably then kill each other in frustration.<br /> <br /> For simplicity's sake, I'd rule that post Basu-Im packmates still have enough Gauru pheromones coming from them that they 'fool' their frenzied packmates.<br /> <br /> *This would be very difficult. I'd say that even dumping them down the bottom of a deep pit, or locking them in a closed room would have the Basu-Im Gauru tearing at the walls trying to escape before they'd focus on their packmates.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T10:08:54-07:00","id":528909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/526167-different-primal-urges-in-basu-im-would-lead-to-dead-pack-members?p=526511#post526511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For simplicity's sake, I'd rule that post Basu-Im packmates still have enough Gauru pheromones coming from them that they 'fool' their frenzied packmates.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is more or less what I was thinking when I first saw the question. Especialy given that they collapse when the rage gives out, by the time your raging Gauru pack mates notice you've stopped raging, they're probably gone.<br /> <br /> Your proposition is a fairly terrifying one, though, and if your players want that to be an option, let it be an option. All I'm saying with the above is that there are easy rationalizations for saying &quot;No, that's not a thing. If we rage together, we are safe from each other.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}